        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
        ":question/problem": "What is the value of $\\frac{2}{5}\\int_{\\frac{e}{4}}^{\\frac{e^{3}}{4}}\\frac{3}{\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)\\operatorname{ln}(4\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right))}\\,\\text{d}x?$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let's set $u=\\ln\\left(4 \\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)\\right).$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}\\,\u27f9\\,1\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $\\frac{e}{4}$ | $\\frac{e^{3}}{4}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $3$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{5}\\int_{\\frac{e}{4}}^{\\frac{e^{3}}{4}}\\frac{3}{\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)\\operatorname{ln}(4\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right))}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ & =\\frac{6}{5}\\int_{\\frac{e}{4}}^{\\frac{e^{3}}{4}}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}(4\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right))}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ & =\\frac{6}{5}\\int_{1}^{3}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot\\left(3(\\operatorname{ln}Abs(u))\\right)|_{1}^{3} \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot\\left(3(\\operatorname{ln}3-\\operatorname{ln}1)\\right) \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot\\left(3\\operatorname{ln}3\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
